Every way an ordering clause can fail to compare — a value that is not a number, a field the row
never declares, an operand that is not a number — excludes the row and leaves the run
successful: the numeric row still comes back, and the unusable operand returns nothing rather
than an error.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/numeric/index.md --
---
title: Numeric
sp: 5
---

body
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/texty/index.md --
---
title: Texty
sp: soon
---

body
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/bare/index.md --
---
title: Bare
---

body
-- cmd --
booping query --glob 'plans/*/index.md' --where sp:gt=0 --output paths
booping query --glob 'plans/*/index.md' --where sp:gt=soon --output paths
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
plans/numeric/index.md
-- stderr --
